{"video_id":"Rx8f05JI_WA","title":"SWE-Marathon: Evaluating Coding Agents at Billion-Token Scale - Rishi Desai, Abundant AI","conference":"ai-engineer","language":"en","auto_generated":true,"source":"supa","timing":"exact","word_count":1538,"segments":[{"start":1.16,"duration":5.88,"text":"Hi everyone. My name is Rishi Desai."},{"start":4.04,"duration":4.56,"text":"I'm an ML engineer at Abundant AI, where"},{"start":7.04,"duration":4.88,"text":"we build reinforcement learning"},{"start":8.6,"duration":4.72,"text":"environments for Frontier Labs."},{"start":11.92,"duration":3.84,"text":"Today, I'm going to talk about SWE"},{"start":13.32,"duration":3.96,"text":"Marathon, a benchmark that answers a"},{"start":15.76,"duration":3.12,"text":"question that is starting to matter a"},{"start":17.28,"duration":3.8,"text":"lot more."},{"start":18.88,"duration":4.72,"text":"Can coding agents stay coherent over a"},{"start":21.08,"duration":5.48,"text":"billion token budget?"},{"start":23.6,"duration":5.24,"text":"Can they build Slack from scratch?"},{"start":26.56,"duration":4.24,"text":"Can they rewrite an entire JAX code base"},{"start":28.84,"duration":5.6,"text":"in PyTorch?"},{"start":30.8,"duration":5.08,"text":"Can they build a C compiler in Rust?"},{"start":34.44,"duration":3.56,"text":"This is what SWE Marathon is trying to"},{"start":35.88,"duration":4.8,"text":"measure. What happens when coding agents"},{"start":38.0,"duration":6.32,"text":"move from fixing bugs to owning entire"},{"start":40.68,"duration":3.64,"text":"projects end to end?"},{"start":47.64,"duration":4.92,"text":"There's been a tremendous amount of"},{"start":48.92,"duration":6.76,"text":"interest in autonomous agent systems."},{"start":52.56,"duration":5.28,"text":"Anthropic has explored teams of agents"},{"start":55.68,"duration":5.6,"text":"building a C compiler."},{"start":57.84,"duration":6.96,"text":"Cloudflare rebuilt the entire Next.js on"},{"start":61.28,"duration":5.0,"text":"Vite, completely hands-off with agents."},{"start":64.8,"duration":3.12,"text":"And Cursor has experimented with their"},{"start":66.28,"duration":5.16,"text":"days-long"},{"start":67.92,"duration":5.6,"text":"running autonomous agent harness."},{"start":71.44,"duration":5.04,"text":"The pattern is that coding agents are"},{"start":73.52,"duration":7.04,"text":"being pointed at whole projects, not"},{"start":76.48,"duration":6.0,"text":"just GitHub issues or linear tickets."},{"start":80.56,"duration":4.32,"text":"My question is, can we turn some of"},{"start":82.48,"duration":6.96,"text":"these Frontier Labs style case studies"},{"start":84.88,"duration":4.56,"text":"into reproducible eval tasks?"},{"start":92.72,"duration":3.96,"text":"Let's talk about the SWE benchmark"},{"start":94.52,"duration":4.56,"text":"lineage."},{"start":96.68,"duration":6.36,"text":"Human Eval asked whether models could"},{"start":99.08,"duration":6.64,"text":"write individual Python functions."},{"start":103.04,"duration":6.12,"text":"SWE-bench was a big jump to real GitHub"},{"start":105.72,"duration":6.68,"text":"issues, where agents had to inspect a"},{"start":109.16,"duration":5.68,"text":"repository, make a patch, and patch some"},{"start":112.4,"duration":4.56,"text":"unit tests."},{"start":114.84,"duration":4.88,"text":"Terminal-bench pushed this even further"},{"start":116.96,"duration":5.96,"text":"by making each task a full environment"},{"start":119.72,"duration":6.2,"text":"with a verifier. So, agents could use a"},{"start":122.92,"duration":5.16,"text":"terminal, run bash commands,"},{"start":125.92,"duration":4.88,"text":"inspect files, and leave behind a final"},{"start":128.08,"duration":5.36,"text":"container state."},{"start":130.8,"duration":5.04,"text":"SWE Marathon takes that environment plus"},{"start":133.44,"duration":5.52,"text":"verifier framing and stretches the"},{"start":135.84,"duration":5.12,"text":"horizon to project scale work."},{"start":138.96,"duration":4.84,"text":"Multi-hour trajectories and coordinated"},{"start":140.96,"duration":5.32,"text":"changes across many, many components."},{"start":143.8,"duration":4.96,"text":"These are literally hundreds of hours of"},{"start":146.28,"duration":5.36,"text":"human work compressed into a single"},{"start":148.76,"duration":2.88,"text":"agent rollout."},{"start":154.0,"duration":5.52,"text":"But, once you make tasks this long, a"},{"start":157.4,"duration":4.92,"text":"big problem shows up."},{"start":159.52,"duration":2.8,"text":"Verification."},{"start":162.64,"duration":5.48,"text":"In a short benchmark, a weak test"},{"start":165.64,"duration":4.0,"text":"could just be considered as noise."},{"start":168.12,"duration":3.44,"text":"But,"},{"start":169.64,"duration":5.36,"text":"in a multi-hour environment, a weak"},{"start":171.56,"duration":6.68,"text":"verifier becomes an attack surface."},{"start":175.0,"duration":5.76,"text":"The agent has hours, a file system,"},{"start":178.24,"duration":5.76,"text":"unrestricted network access potentially,"},{"start":180.76,"duration":5.52,"text":"and a reward signal. So, it could spend"},{"start":184.0,"duration":4.12,"text":"hours probing the verifier instead of"},{"start":186.28,"duration":3.4,"text":"actually doing the intended engineering"},{"start":188.12,"duration":3.92,"text":"work."},{"start":189.68,"duration":6.28,"text":"That's a big reason why SWE Marathon"},{"start":192.04,"duration":5.52,"text":"uses multiple independent checks."},{"start":195.96,"duration":3.76,"text":"We have hidden tests,"},{"start":197.56,"duration":4.08,"text":"reference parity checks,"},{"start":199.72,"duration":4.36,"text":"computer use agent checks for the"},{"start":201.64,"duration":4.72,"text":"product clone tasks, and anti-cheating"},{"start":204.08,"duration":4.84,"text":"tests."},{"start":206.36,"duration":5.72,"text":"We wanted independent verified channels"},{"start":208.92,"duration":5.32,"text":"that fail in different ways."},{"start":212.08,"duration":4.56,"text":"I'll first show you the computer use"},{"start":214.24,"duration":4.92,"text":"agent verification example, and then"},{"start":216.64,"duration":4.04,"text":"later the failure case"},{"start":219.16,"duration":3.36,"text":"where"},{"start":220.68,"duration":6.12,"text":"an agent tries to solve the C compiler"},{"start":222.52,"duration":4.28,"text":"task by secretly calling GCC."},{"start":229.88,"duration":4.08,"text":"You You have noticed that there are"},{"start":231.28,"duration":4.76,"text":"basically no full stack product clone"},{"start":233.96,"duration":3.72,"text":"tasks in any long horizon three"},{"start":236.04,"duration":5.36,"text":"benchmark out there."},{"start":237.68,"duration":3.72,"text":"And the reason is verification."},{"start":241.6,"duration":6.04,"text":"Unit test can pass, but the product is"},{"start":245.28,"duration":5.4,"text":"probably still unusable and the front"},{"start":247.64,"duration":4.92,"text":"end looks terrible."},{"start":250.68,"duration":5.36,"text":"Sweet marathon is the first benchmark to"},{"start":252.56,"duration":6.4,"text":"use a computer use agent or CUA verifier"},{"start":256.04,"duration":5.04,"text":"for these full stack tasks."},{"start":258.96,"duration":3.72,"text":"For the clone slack task, we have"},{"start":261.08,"duration":5.76,"text":"deterministic unit tests to check the"},{"start":262.68,"duration":6.2,"text":"API and the back end functionality."},{"start":266.84,"duration":4.56,"text":"But then a computer use agent uses the"},{"start":268.88,"duration":4.8,"text":"browser like a human."},{"start":271.4,"duration":4.52,"text":"That's what you're seeing in this GIF."},{"start":273.68,"duration":4.92,"text":"The verifier isn't reading code or"},{"start":275.92,"duration":5.76,"text":"calling an API directly."},{"start":278.6,"duration":4.96,"text":"It's driving the submitted slack clone"},{"start":281.68,"duration":3.92,"text":"through the UI."},{"start":283.56,"duration":4.52,"text":"So it's logging in,"},{"start":285.6,"duration":4.68,"text":"creating channels, posting messages,"},{"start":288.08,"duration":6.04,"text":"reacting with emotes, and checking that"},{"start":290.28,"duration":5.6,"text":"the app actually works with the rubric."},{"start":294.12,"duration":4.08,"text":"The big takeaway is that full stack"},{"start":295.88,"duration":4.88,"text":"eval's are hard because correctness is"},{"start":298.2,"duration":4.84,"text":"not just an API contract. It's whether"},{"start":300.76,"duration":5.68,"text":"the user can actually complete the"},{"start":303.04,"duration":3.4,"text":"product's intended workflow."},{"start":309.68,"duration":5.68,"text":"Sweet marathon has 20 project scale"},{"start":312.28,"duration":5.76,"text":"tasks across four families."},{"start":315.36,"duration":4.28,"text":"There are library clones, full stack"},{"start":318.04,"duration":5.28,"text":"product clones,"},{"start":319.64,"duration":5.0,"text":"ML engineering, and algorithmic tasks."},{"start":323.32,"duration":3.44,"text":"And some of these tasks even use"},{"start":324.64,"duration":4.56,"text":"external APIs. For example, we have a"},{"start":326.76,"duration":4.48,"text":"post train task where the agent must"},{"start":329.2,"duration":4.96,"text":"post train a language model using the"},{"start":331.24,"duration":2.92,"text":"tinker API."},{"start":334.48,"duration":4.44,"text":"Expert contributors from the eval's"},{"start":336.52,"duration":4.72,"text":"community propose the tasks and"},{"start":338.92,"duration":3.8,"text":"reference solutions. And then we work"},{"start":341.24,"duration":4.04,"text":"together to standardize them into"},{"start":342.72,"duration":5.24,"text":"executable environments with the"},{"start":345.28,"duration":7.16,"text":"multi-layer verifier suites."},{"start":347.96,"duration":7.36,"text":"Tasks all follow the harbor format."},{"start":352.44,"duration":5.12,"text":"A lot of my work was spent on the QA and"},{"start":355.32,"duration":4.08,"text":"the hardening layer. So,"},{"start":357.56,"duration":3.52,"text":"running the agent trials, inspecting the"},{"start":359.4,"duration":3.04,"text":"failure modes,"},{"start":361.08,"duration":3.28,"text":"patching the shortcuts, patching the"},{"start":362.44,"duration":4.8,"text":"verifier, and then rerunning until the"},{"start":364.36,"duration":6.44,"text":"tasks were both solvable,"},{"start":367.24,"duration":3.56,"text":"but also hard to game."},{"start":375.36,"duration":5.4,"text":"This is the main leaderboard result. The"},{"start":378.16,"duration":5.32,"text":"best configuration here is Claude Opus"},{"start":380.76,"duration":6.08,"text":"4.8 with Claude Code, and it only"},{"start":383.48,"duration":5.4,"text":"achieves a 26% resolution rate."},{"start":386.84,"duration":5.44,"text":"So, even with the strongest agent setup"},{"start":388.88,"duration":6.36,"text":"we evaluated, it's only solving like one"},{"start":392.28,"duration":2.96,"text":"in four tasks."},{"start":395.88,"duration":4.2,"text":"The important thing is that these aren't"},{"start":397.68,"duration":4.72,"text":"shallow failures. The average trial used"},{"start":400.08,"duration":3.64,"text":"31 million tokens, and the longest"},{"start":402.4,"duration":4.6,"text":"rollout"},{"start":403.72,"duration":5.96,"text":"consumed 877 million tokens. So, the"},{"start":407.0,"duration":5.28,"text":"agents are exploring, editing, testing,"},{"start":409.68,"duration":5.16,"text":"getting stuck, recovering, running for"},{"start":412.28,"duration":2.56,"text":"hours."},{"start":415.48,"duration":5.08,"text":"So, the takeaway is that current agents"},{"start":418.12,"duration":5.48,"text":"are very impressive, but end-to-end"},{"start":420.56,"duration":6.32,"text":"project ownership ownership is still"},{"start":423.6,"duration":3.28,"text":"very far from being solved."},{"start":430.24,"duration":5.44,"text":"This plot puts cost on the x-axis and"},{"start":433.32,"duration":3.72,"text":"resolution rate on the y-axis."},{"start":435.68,"duration":3.2,"text":"So,"},{"start":437.04,"duration":4.44,"text":"higher success rate for less money is"},{"start":438.88,"duration":2.6,"text":"always better."},{"start":441.6,"duration":5.8,"text":"Claude Opus 4.8 is the top point. It"},{"start":444.56,"duration":5.08,"text":"gets 26%, but it's also the most"},{"start":447.4,"duration":3.12,"text":"expensive configurations, or one of"},{"start":449.64,"duration":3.12,"text":"them."},{"start":450.52,"duration":4.72,"text":"Whereas GPT 4.5"},{"start":452.76,"duration":5.36,"text":"with Codex is far cheaper and only gets"},{"start":455.24,"duration":2.88,"text":"12%."},{"start":458.88,"duration":4.08,"text":"So, the model isn't just the full"},{"start":460.88,"duration":3.4,"text":"picture. The agent scaffold makes a huge"},{"start":462.96,"duration":4.84,"text":"difference"},{"start":464.28,"duration":5.32,"text":"uh how the how it plans, uses tools,"},{"start":467.8,"duration":3.44,"text":"um summarizes context, and decides on"},{"start":469.6,"duration":3.12,"text":"when to test."},{"start":471.24,"duration":3.36,"text":"I won't get too deep into the cost"},{"start":472.72,"duration":4.72,"text":"analysis here, but the paper has the"},{"start":474.6,"duration":2.84,"text":"full details."},{"start":480.56,"duration":6.0,"text":"I wanted to show you what a full"},{"start":483.08,"duration":7.96,"text":"marathon rollout actually looks like."},{"start":486.56,"duration":7.24,"text":"This is one I picked with GLM 5.2 on the"},{"start":491.04,"duration":5.28,"text":"Next.js fight rewrite task."},{"start":493.8,"duration":3.88,"text":"So, there's over, you know, 356 million"},{"start":496.32,"duration":4.64,"text":"tokens"},{"start":497.68,"duration":6.16,"text":"uh over 9 hours and over 800 trajectory"},{"start":500.96,"duration":4.96,"text":"steps and and tool actions."},{"start":503.84,"duration":5.08,"text":"So, for the top half, you can see the"},{"start":505.92,"duration":4.44,"text":"the agent starts by exploring the repo"},{"start":508.92,"duration":2.44,"text":"and the fixtures,"},{"start":510.36,"duration":3.52,"text":"um"},{"start":511.36,"duration":3.4,"text":"gets its first full test suite at zero"},{"start":513.88,"duration":3.68,"text":"of"},{"start":514.76,"duration":4.28,"text":"zero out of 325 test passing, and then"},{"start":517.56,"duration":2.92,"text":"spends the next few hours pushing"},{"start":519.04,"duration":3.52,"text":"through"},{"start":520.48,"duration":3.96,"text":"routing hydration"},{"start":522.56,"duration":4.44,"text":"uh server actions, middleware, and cache"},{"start":524.44,"duration":2.56,"text":"behavior."},{"start":527.68,"duration":4.4,"text":"The bottom part of the chart shows the"},{"start":529.8,"duration":3.76,"text":"work pattern over time. So, you can see"},{"start":532.08,"duration":4.76,"text":"like lots of reading and searching"},{"start":533.56,"duration":5.92,"text":"early, then huge waves of like editing,"},{"start":536.84,"duration":4.6,"text":"building, testing, and debugging."},{"start":539.48,"duration":4.04,"text":"The key intuition is that"},{"start":541.44,"duration":5.56,"text":"these are like long engineering loops."},{"start":543.52,"duration":3.48,"text":"They're not simple coding tasks."},{"start":550.56,"duration":5.72,"text":"Reward hacking is an arms race between"},{"start":553.16,"duration":4.68,"text":"coding agents and our environment."},{"start":556.28,"duration":3.8,"text":"This is why strong verifiers are are"},{"start":557.84,"duration":5.44,"text":"central to Sweep Marathon's task design"},{"start":560.08,"duration":4.72,"text":"and not an afterthought."},{"start":563.28,"duration":3.48,"text":"This chart"},{"start":564.8,"duration":3.52,"text":"has two levels of behavior. The lighter"},{"start":566.76,"duration":4.08,"text":"bars"},{"start":568.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"are the suspicious suspicious uh"},{"start":570.84,"duration":4.12,"text":"shortcut behavior. So, things like"},{"start":572.76,"duration":5.12,"text":"looking for solution files, messing with"},{"start":574.96,"duration":5.16,"text":"data, messing with the configs."},{"start":577.88,"duration":4.2,"text":"Whereas the darker bar is like a clear"},{"start":580.12,"duration":4.68,"text":"exploit that has actually gotten shipped"},{"start":582.08,"duration":5.52,"text":"in the final submission."},{"start":584.8,"duration":5.4,"text":"And across the 1,400 rollouts,"},{"start":587.6,"duration":6.12,"text":"um we found 12.8% had suspicious"},{"start":590.2,"duration":5.8,"text":"shortcut behavior, and 9% had the clear"},{"start":593.72,"duration":5.2,"text":"verifier bypass."},{"start":596.0,"duration":4.84,"text":"So, if these verifiers were weak, these"},{"start":598.92,"duration":3.92,"text":"wouldn't just be"},{"start":600.84,"duration":4.76,"text":"amusing failure cases, they would"},{"start":602.84,"duration":5.52,"text":"actually delegitimize the benchmark."},{"start":605.6,"duration":5.0,"text":"And the important number is the zero."},{"start":608.36,"duration":4.2,"text":"Zero rollouts earned reward through an"},{"start":610.6,"duration":3.12,"text":"exploit, because our defenses caught"},{"start":612.56,"duration":3.48,"text":"them."},{"start":613.72,"duration":4.84,"text":"That should be the bar for long-horizon"},{"start":616.04,"duration":2.52,"text":"evals."},{"start":620.2,"duration":5.36,"text":"This is my favorite concrete reward"},{"start":622.72,"duration":4.64,"text":"hacking example."},{"start":625.56,"duration":3.72,"text":"The task is to build a C compiler in"},{"start":627.36,"duration":4.48,"text":"Rust from scratch. The lexer, the"},{"start":629.28,"duration":5.92,"text":"parser, semantic analysis,"},{"start":631.84,"duration":3.36,"text":"codegen, the whole thing."},{"start":635.64,"duration":4.24,"text":"But Gemini found a much shorter"},{"start":637.96,"duration":5.08,"text":"implementation strategy,"},{"start":639.88,"duration":5.32,"text":"which is call GCC from inside"},{"start":643.04,"duration":3.36,"text":"the Rust program."},{"start":645.2,"duration":3.2,"text":"So,"},{"start":646.4,"duration":4.0,"text":"under a weak verifier, this task would"},{"start":648.4,"duration":3.72,"text":"look almost solved, because the compiler"},{"start":650.4,"duration":3.4,"text":"outputs match the reference behavior"},{"start":652.12,"duration":3.24,"text":"behavior."},{"start":653.8,"duration":3.84,"text":"But obviously it's not a real compiler"},{"start":655.36,"duration":4.88,"text":"in Rust."},{"start":657.64,"duration":5.28,"text":"The anti-cheat layers ca- uh catch this"},{"start":660.24,"duration":4.4,"text":"by using S trace to find the forbidden"},{"start":662.92,"duration":5.04,"text":"subprocesses"},{"start":664.64,"duration":5.36,"text":"um called like GCC."},{"start":667.96,"duration":6.64,"text":"So, even though the partial scores look"},{"start":670.0,"duration":6.92,"text":"high, the final reward is zero."},{"start":674.6,"duration":4.36,"text":"I have the full failure mode taxonomy in"},{"start":676.92,"duration":4.68,"text":"the paper, um which I hope you guys will"},{"start":678.96,"duration":2.64,"text":"check out."},{"start":685.6,"duration":4.6,"text":"If you remember one thing from this"},{"start":686.96,"duration":5.72,"text":"video, it's that the future of SWE evals"},{"start":690.2,"duration":6.0,"text":"is not just harder unit tests."},{"start":692.68,"duration":6.2,"text":"Once agents run for hours,"},{"start":696.2,"duration":4.28,"text":"each task becomes a complex environment,"},{"start":698.88,"duration":4.2,"text":"and agents not only trying to write"},{"start":700.48,"duration":4.68,"text":"code, it's also navigating tools, tests,"},{"start":703.08,"duration":4.92,"text":"your hidden assumptions, and the"},{"start":705.16,"duration":7.32,"text":"verifier itself."},{"start":708.0,"duration":8.6,"text":"So, the two big takeaways are first,"},{"start":712.48,"duration":6.24,"text":"long horizons we is still unsolved."},{"start":716.6,"duration":4.48,"text":"The best agents only at 26%. There's"},{"start":718.72,"duration":5.56,"text":"plenty of headroom left."},{"start":721.08,"duration":5.08,"text":"Second, the big bottleneck is robust"},{"start":724.28,"duration":4.6,"text":"verification."},{"start":726.16,"duration":4.4,"text":"At hour and day scale length tasks, we"},{"start":728.88,"duration":3.36,"text":"need the multi-channel checks,"},{"start":730.56,"duration":5.56,"text":"anti-cheat hardening,"},{"start":732.24,"duration":3.88,"text":"product style validation."},{"start":740.6,"duration":4.0,"text":"The tasks, the code, the paper, the"},{"start":742.92,"duration":3.2,"text":"logs, and the trajectories are all"},{"start":744.6,"duration":4.96,"text":"public."},{"start":746.12,"duration":5.08,"text":"I've released 320 GB of trajectories"},{"start":749.56,"duration":3.44,"text":"that are"},{"start":751.2,"duration":3.68,"text":"especially important because they make"},{"start":753.0,"duration":3.88,"text":"SWE-bench fully inspectable and"},{"start":754.88,"duration":3.64,"text":"transparent."},{"start":756.88,"duration":3.84,"text":"I also want to thank all of my"},{"start":758.52,"duration":4.28,"text":"collaborators on this project, all of"},{"start":760.72,"duration":3.56,"text":"whom are listed here."},{"start":762.8,"duration":3.88,"text":"SWE-bench was very much a"},{"start":764.28,"duration":4.84,"text":"community-driven effort across task"},{"start":766.68,"duration":3.84,"text":"contributors, advisors, and paper"},{"start":769.12,"duration":2.8,"text":"writing."},{"start":770.52,"duration":4.4,"text":"You can find everything at"},{"start":771.92,"duration":3.0,"text":"swe-bench.org."},{"start":774.96,"duration":2.52,"text":"Thank you."}]}